            "value": 2
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You recite an excerpt of the Laws of Mortality, often the first law: \"Let no mortal be beholden to a god.\" Attempt an @Check[intimidation|against:will] check against all enemies within 60 feet that worship a deity, comparing your result against each target's Will DC. Targets are then temporarily immune to your use of this ability for 24 hours.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Frightened]{Frightened 2}. Until the start of your next turn, if the target attempts to Cast a Spell with the divine trait, it must succeed at a @Check[flat|dc:7] or the action is lost.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Frightened]{Frightened 1}, and the DC of the flat check is 5.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect: Edict of Mortality]</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 8
          },
